# Luminary marker — brass chip + condensed figlet
- date: 2026-11-06
- branch: feat/brass-mark
- lead: jony-ive — material honesty. A terminal is a character grid, not a
  bitmap. The old mark pretended otherwise and broke on contact. The cure is
  to use the medium as what it is: letterforms made of letters.
- supporting: ellen-lupton (type is a voice carried by weight and rhythm —
  the figlet and the chip are the same voice at two sizes), vitaly-friedman
  (whitespace is load-bearing — the chip's padding is what makes it a mark
  rather than coloured text)
- deferred-lens: michael-bierut argued for the real clef glyph as a
  generative mark. Operator deferred it to cli#475; the reasoning is recorded
  there rather than lost.
